          "text": "# Using Langfuse TypeScript SDK for LLM Tracking\n\nThe Langfuse TypeScript SDK provides multiple approaches to track LLM calls and conversations:\n\n## Setup\n\nFirst, configure your environment variables:\n```typescript\nprocess.env.LANGFUSE_PUBLIC_KEY = \"pk-lf-***\";\nprocess.env.LANGFUSE_SECRET_KEY = \"sk-lf-***\";\nprocess.env.LANGFUSE_BASE_URL = \"https://cloud.langfuse.com\";\nprocess.env.OPENAI_API_KEY = \"sk-proj-***\";\n```\n\nInitialize the SDK with OpenTelemetry:\n```typescript\nimport { NodeSDK } from \"@opentelemetry/sdk-node\";\nimport { LangfuseSpanProcessor } from \"@langfuse/otel\";\n\nconst langfuseSpanProcessor = new LangfuseSpanProcessor({\n  publicKey: process.env.LANGFUSE_PUBLIC_KEY!,\n  secretKey: process.env.LANGFUSE_SECRET_KEY!,\n});\n\nconst sdk = new NodeSDK({\n  spanProcessors: [langfuseSpanProcessor],\n});\nsdk.start();\n```\n\n## Three Main Tracing Methods\n\n### 1. **Context Manager** (Recommended)\nBest for \"automatic context management\" and preventing \"context leakage\":\n\n```typescript\nimport { startActiveObservation, startObservation } from \"@langfuse/tracing\";\n\nawait startActiveObservation(\"query-handler\", async (span) => {\n  span.update({ input: { query: \"What is Paris?\" } });\n  \n  const generation = startObservation(\n    \"llm-call\",\n    { model: \"gpt-4\", input: [{ role: \"user\", content: \"...\" }] },\n    { asType: \"generation\" }\n  );\n  \n  generation.update({ output: { content: \"Paris is the capital...\" } }).end();\n});\n```\n\n### 2. **Observe Decorator**\nTrace functions automatically without modifying their logic:\n\n```typescript\nimport { observe } from \"@langfuse/tracing\";\n\nconst tracedFunction = observe(myFunction, {\n  name: \"my-operation\",\n  asType: \"generation\",\n});\n\nawait tracedFunction(args);\n```\n\n### 3. **Manual Spans**\nFor granular control over span creation and nesting:\n\n```typescript\nconst span = startObservation('root-operation', { input: {...} });\n\nconst toolCall = span.startObservation(\n  'fetch-data',\n  { input: { query: '...' } },\n  { asType: \"tool\" }\n);\n\ntoolCall.update({ output: {...} }).end();\nspan.end();\n```\n\n## Native Integrations\n\nFor automatic parameter capture, use framework-specific integrations:\n\n- **OpenAI**: `observeOpenAI()` wraps the client\n- **LangChain**: `CallbackHandler` for automatic tracing\n- **Vercel AI SDK**: Enable with `experimental_telemetry: {isEnabled: true}`\n\nAll approaches support token usage tracking, custom metadata, user/session IDs, and hierarchical span relationships for multi-turn conversations.",
